--- a/docs/plugins/sdk-runtime/channel.md
+++ b/docs/plugins/sdk-runtime/channel.md
@@ -198,3 +198,30 @@ lifecycle setters still require their own persistence migrations. Other bundled
 stores also retain their existing behavior until their respective cutovers.
 Worker-backed route reads and activity updates do not imply a fully migrated
 binding service or stronger durability for those remaining operations.
+
+
+## Isolated v1 turn-display extension seam
+
+The Telegram display bridge prototype for base `e178c39` uses
+`api.runtime.channel.runtimeContexts.get({ channelId: "telegram", capability })`.
+The two capability keys are `finalUsageFooter.v1` (reviewed owner
+`token-speed-footer`) and `ordinaryToolProgress.v1` (`compact-telegram-progress`).
+They are loader-instance-bound, not authenticated by a caller-supplied plugin ID.
+Registration requires the actual API lifecycle signal and returns a disposal lease;
+raw registry replacement of these host-owned keys is refused.
+
+The host snapshots the one published plugin generation for each admitted Telegram
+turn. Replacement registrations can be staged before publication but cannot adopt
+old turns. The formatter receives official whole-turn aggregate usage and wall
+duration, returns bounded literal text, and does not register a modifying send hook.
+Undefined, exceptions, malformed output, cancellation or retirement retain native
+behavior. The reducer sees only public call/name/phase/status summaries and returns
+at most three bounded ordinary category rows; approval, plan, reasoning, headline
+and final message custody remain native. Native direct callbacks carry an opaque
+per-event projection token into the serialized compositor queue, avoiding
+concurrent same-call or different-call handoff loss. No transport client, token,
+message edit/delete authority or ingress elevation is exposed to the helpers.
+
+This patch is not part of an installed/live Gateway until separately built,
+reviewed and deployed by its operator. Synthetic transport tests are actual host
+integration evidence, not live Telegram acceptance.
